  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.attr.aria.label.75986eb0a809": "Codex unlock status",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.attr.aria.label.ded422b06fbe": "Play signal",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.12b46c981beb": "Concord administrator. Vale appears through forwarded paperwork, authorization codes, and systems that make refusal more expensive than compliance.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.2115ae690db0": "Bourse freight seal clerk. When the verification database agrees with the cargo seal, the seal becomes the story everyone else must use.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.245f36bd10ea": "Cargo registrar tied to the 47-A weight variance. If a manifest changes mass, his initials usually survive the transfer.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.4f96a80f3a52": "Pit Engineering maintenance worker attached to the recycler report. The bounty paperwork called him hostile; the ledger says why that mattered.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.56ff094d1979": "The Ashfall figure. His station is less a confession than a ledger that kept running after everyone else left.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.6d641e453740": "Drift claim recorder. Exhausted claims have a way of becoming fresh again for the crew that files second.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.815c4d432ebf": "Wren, current pilot of the Tessera. Concord Registry still lists the operator as UNKNOWN; the ship knows better than the paperwork.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.90b60f8686c5": "Outpost bar proprietor. Rates stay posted, management keeps changing, and the drawer always closes on the same count.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.91d34c75c461": "Bounty broker. A clean tag is useful because it can be billed twice before anyone asks which target was real.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.c269f584d2fb": "Gate 3 customs officer. Hale does not need to open a sealed hold; he only needs to file the second fine correctly.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.body.d9724c5f3170": "Shipyard welder. His repairs look official because they are signed official, which is not the same as safe.",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.title.17d8e6c91e0f": "Anomaly Contact",
  "loc.src.ui.screens.codex.field.title.67e73362682d": "Gate Approach",
